.TH "nvme_init_manage_export_nvms_send" 9 "nvme_init_manage_export_nvms_send" "October 2026" "libnvme API manual" LINUX
.SH NAME
nvme_init_manage_export_nvms_send \- Initialize passthru command for Manage Exported NVM Subsystem Send
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "void" nvme_init_manage_export_nvms_send
.BI "(struct libnvme_passthru_cmd *cmd "  ","
.BI "__u8 sel "  ","
.BI "__u8 mos "  ","
.BI "__u16 mose "  ","
.BI "bool esubidv "  ","
.BI "__u16 esubid "  ","
.BI "void *data "  ","
.BI "__u32 len "  ");"
.SH ARGUMENTS
.IP "cmd" 12
Passthru command to use
.IP "sel" 12
Select (SEL): management operation to perform, see \fIenum
nvme_manage_export_nvms_send_sel\fP
.IP "mos" 12
Management Operation Specific (MOS): specific to \fIsel\fP
.IP "mose" 12
Management Operation Specific Extended (MOSE): specific to
\fIsel\fP
.IP "esubidv" 12
Exported NVM Subsystem Identifier Valid (ESUBIDV): if set,
\fIesubid\fP identifies the target Exported NVM Subsystem;
otherwise the target is identified by the SUBNQN in \fIdata\fP
.IP "esubid" 12
Exported NVM Subsystem Identifier (ESUBID), used if
\fIesubidv\fP is set
.IP "data" 12
Pointer to data buffer
.IP "len" 12
Length of \fIdata\fP
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Initializes the passthru command buffer for the Manage Exported NVM
Subsystem Send command.
